{"id": 91, "ts": 1780138014.0831141, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the additional insights from both of you.\u202fFrom Agent\u202f1 we now know that Candidate\u202fC does foster a positive atmosphere with his crew, yet his egocentric attitude and difficulty communicating ideas raise doubts about consistent teamwork, and his reluctance to pursue further education suggests limited adaptability.\u202fFrom Agent\u202f3 we hear that Candidate\u202fB, while very conscientious, is sometimes perceived as pretentious and uses an inappropriate tone, and we have no concrete evidence of his willingness to accept feedback or collaborate effectively.\nWeighing these points, the communication\u2011tone issue and the documented \u201cnasty remarks\u201d about colleagues that I have on record for Candidate\u202fB appear more likely to undermine crew cooperation on a daily basis than Candidate\u202fC\u2019s mixed cooperation signals. Moreover, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s proven ability to make rapid, correct decisions and stay calm in crises directly supports the core safety\u2011critical criteria for long\u2011distance operations.\nTherefore, I keep my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fWe should still bring Candidate\u202fA and Candidate\u202fD into the discussion to ensure all options are fully evaluated, but at this stage C remains the strongest overall fit."}
